  "term": "HRNB",
  "definition": "HRNB stands for high-risk neuroblastoma, a more aggressive form of neuroblastoma discussed in pediatric oncology. In this source, it is one of the pediatric solid tumors for which high-dose chemotherapy followed by autologous stem-cell transplantation has been used.",
